@startuml codeemb-cache
' CodeEmbeddingCache: key derivation splits on code length (gxhash needs a 16-byte
' SIMD floor), the DashMap probe is lock-free, and the capacity guard evicts an
' ARBITRARY entry chosen by iteration order — not the least-recently-used one.
' Render: plantuml -tsvg docs/diagrams/codeemb-cache.puml
' Source of truth for Figure 1 in docs/components/code-embeddings/caching.md.
skinparam backgroundColor #FAFAFA
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam defaultTextAlignment center
skinparam linetype ortho
skinparam rectangle {
  FontColor white
  FontStyle bold
  BorderColor #263238
  roundCorner 12
}
skinparam ArrowColor #37474F
skinparam ArrowFontColor #37474F
title CodeEmbeddingCache — key derivation, probe, and arbitrary-victim eviction

rectangle "**(code c, language ℓ)**" as q #EF6C00

rectangle "**compute_key(c, ℓ)**\nsplit on len(c) vs GXHASH_MIN_SIZE = 16" as key #00838F
rectangle "**len(c) ≥ 16**\nGxHasher: c.hash() then ℓ.hash()\n(AES-accelerated, 16-byte SIMD reads)" as long #00838F
rectangle "**len(c) < 16**\nh = FNV-1a(c bytes)\nh ⊕= ℓ as u64;  h ×= FNV_PRIME" as short #00838F
rectangle "**key ∈ u64**" as k #006064

rectangle "**DashMap⟨u64, Arc[f32]⟩**\nsharded — lock-free reads" as map #00838F

rectangle "**HIT**\nArc::clone (refcount bump)\n…then .to_vec() at the trait\nboundary copies it anyway" as hit #455A64
rectangle "**MISS**\ntokenize → ONNX → pool → normalize\n(the expensive path)" as miss #2E7D32

rectangle "**insert**\nlen() ≥ max_entries (10 000)?" as ins #00838F
rectangle "**Evict**  cache.iter().next()\n⇒ an **arbitrary** entry\n(iteration order, not recency)" as evict #90A4AE

q --> key
key --> long
key --> short
long --> k
short --> k
k --> map : get(&key)
map --> hit
map --> miss
miss --> ins
ins --> evict : at capacity
evict --> map : remove(victim)
ins --> map : insert(key, Arc::from(v))
map --> hit : after insert

note bottom of evict #ECEFF1
  **Not LRU, not truly random.** The victim is
  whatever DashMap's iterator yields first. Model the
  hit ratio as RANDOM replacement, never as LRU.
  The len()-then-insert guard is also **racy**: k
  concurrent inserters can push the map k−1 entries
  past max_entries before any of them evicts.
end note

note right of map #E0F2F1
  No code is stored beside the key, so a
  64-bit collision **silently** returns the
  wrong embedding. At n = 10⁴ entries the
  birthday bound is ≈ 2.7 × 10⁻¹² — see (C6).
end note

note left of key #FFF3E0
  ""CodeEmbeddingCacheConfig::hash_keys""
  exists and is **never read**: keys are
  always hashed.
end note

@enduml
